WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.440
Mechanized Attack.

00:00:01.820 --> 00:00:05.540
At first, it looked like just another revolution.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:30.780
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.700
I'm Mike. I'm Sean.

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:34.040
And I'm Joe.

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:39.920
Mechanized. It only looked like just another revolution.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:43.280
At first, it looked like just another revolution.

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:49.260
That sounds like it could have been the start of an 80s love ballad or something.

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:51.340
It's very poetic.

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:52.180
I like it.

00:00:52.360 --> 00:01:03.900
The game is about a revolution where the rebel forces are backed by a technology company, I

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:07.460
suppose, that can put robots inside their bodies or something.

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:08.840
They're backed by Uber.

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:10.420
Yeah. Right.

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:17.240
And so the threat is that if this revolution succeeds, the safety of the entire world may

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:22.840
be threatened. Have we ever played a game where you're trying to shut down a revolution?

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:27.460
Like, I mean, like where the people are revolting against the government and you're supposed to

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:29.340
be like, we got to kill all these rebels.

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:34.240
Is there anything in the manual that is like who these rebels are?

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:35.740
What they're revolting against?

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:38.380
It's just rebels and it's just a revolution.

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:41.260
Yep. It does not mention a state.

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:48.060
But yeah, this is, you are acting on behalf of the state to put down the will of the people.

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:52.780
However, many of those people may or may not be cyborgs is neither here nor there.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:56.860
Well, that was, that was a big, big thought for me though.

00:01:56.940 --> 00:02:00.080
Because it's like, some of them are cyborgs or are they robots?

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:02.840
Like I couldn't tell because then there's other ones that aren't.

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:06.420
So it's like, what? Some of them are definitely just people.

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:08.020
Yeah. Some of them are just people.

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:13.740
And then occasionally you'll have to like shoot one twice because it, it removes its

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:15.680
flesh and shows its robot.

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:21.720
But all dogs, all dogs are robots and they won't go to heaven.

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:22.560
They won't go to heaven.

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:24.020
That's a crazy plot.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:28.480
And I think we'll leave it there before it gets any more political and just move on

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:32.160
to the absolutely insane cover for this game.

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:36.120
Guys, do yourself a favor and just look up mechanized attack box art.

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:37.680
Make sure you're looking at the NES one.

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:40.880
Cause it's just, it's from the POV of the player.

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:48.460
You see your arms, but honestly, it could look like your feet depending on how you curl your toes.

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:59.040
It's your arms holding a machine gun, blasting away at wolves to your left, a guy in scuba gear, rushing at you from the right.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:03.660
A bunch of what looks like people like on a hunt.

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:09.360
Like they don't necessarily look like they're what they want to be in the line of fire and military combat.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:11.140
They were just hunting with those wolves.

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:13.300
And now they've got involved in this.

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:20.940
And then just like a giant Mac, another giant Mac, a helicopter, another helicopter.

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:22.560
Like this is insane.

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:24.580
This is insane cover.

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:33.900
Just to add to it, the, there's just like a bunch of extra like metal around the, the title, like holding it in place or something.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:35.520
No, no, no. That's not, that's not just metal.

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:36.560
That's what I was going to say.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:40.280
That the logo is fashioned to look like an Uzi.

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:41.940
Yes, it is. Oh, wow.

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:43.820
Didn't, didn't see it until just now.

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:48.300
It's very, it's very above and beyond.

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:58.000
And do you know why the Uzi is such a prominent thing here, both on like what the POV character is holding and the mechanized attack logo?

00:03:58.320 --> 00:03:59.280
Why don't you tell us?

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:03.540
It, well, it's because presumably that's what you're shooting in the game too, right?

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:05.120
It is a rapid fire gun.

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:08.320
Um, but it's also in the arcade version.

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:13.760
You actually had like a little, you know, a little Uzi that you would be able to.

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:15.900
An Uzi. Yeah.

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:18.400
Cause it was, it was shrunk down.

00:04:18.580 --> 00:04:23.600
It wasn't to scale, but a little Uzi that, uh, you see, you got me saying made up words.

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:25.500
Half the time. I'm not even making them up.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:32.180
Uh, the, the machine gun or Uzi had a little bit of a recoil to it.

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:36.220
I think that's really neat for 1989, 90.

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:44.320
I don't know when it came to the arcades, but, uh, a game that early that, uh, while, even if you're just holding it down and it's constantly firing,

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:47.900
you're going to feel a little bit of feedback on that.

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:54.940
And, uh, it's not even, it's not even the first game to have an Uzi as like the thing that you use to control.

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:58.920
That would go to another NES game that at one point was essential.

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:09.080
Operation Wolf was the first in the, uh, Uzi arcade game, shoot them ups, uh, or shooters, light gun shooter games.

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:14.760
Uh, and now here we are mechanized attack going all in on it.

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:18.320
What do we think about this arcade shooter?

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:21.580
Well, so I have a, I have something.

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:32.420
So it's funny that it's sort of the whole, uh, branding of this game is around that Uzi or Uzi teeny.

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:43.360
Um, and it is one of these games that you can play either with the controller, um, and just sort of use the D pad as a cursor.

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:46.160
And that's where you shoot and you will shoot automatic.

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:49.020
Like it is fully like you're, you're shooting.

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:50.300
You hold the button down.

00:05:50.440 --> 00:05:51.280
You will continue to shoot.

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:54.840
And the arcade game had that Uzi.

00:05:55.060 --> 00:05:57.920
You held the button, you hold the trigger down, you continue to shoot.

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:05.280
And for a weird, for some weird reason, and I think it has to do with the fact that like, just how the light gun works.

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:09.260
When you use that, you, it's all single shot.

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:11.480
You have to tap every time you fire.

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:20.520
And I think like, that's such a weird, like compromise that they had to make for a game where the way that you fire is so central to the game.

00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:27.100
So Sean, you're making me believe that you played it, uh, with a zapper or whatever light gun equivalent.

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:28.140
I did not.

00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:29.740
I read that in the manual.

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:40.280
Oh, I was gonna say, because it is a game that allows you to choose whether you want to play with a zapper or with a standard NES controller.

00:06:41.060 --> 00:06:43.360
That is a crazy choice to give people.

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:51.920
I, I guess it's because it's coming from a third party company that they didn't want to force you to buy Nintendo accessories.

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:56.780
Cause SNK wasn't putting out their own, or maybe they were, but I don't know that that wouldn't make sense.

00:06:56.780 --> 00:06:59.100
But they're, they're allowing you the option to play with a controller.

00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:04.820
And that's really where, like, that's where the bulk of this conversation is going to go, right?

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:18.940
Like, it's just, it's an entirely different game when you're playing with a, a D pad where you, you know, you're, you have like a cursor moving around the screen and it moves very fast and very rigidly and not accurate at all.

00:07:18.940 --> 00:07:24.380
Versus a NES zapper where you can literally just duck hunt this thing.

00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:27.160
And if you point to it, you'll shoot them right away.

00:07:28.700 --> 00:07:32.880
Obviously I'm kind of saying what I preferred, but I did try both.

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:41.520
And I gotta say, I think, uh, what I'm laying down here is just the truth that the controller is the inferior option.

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:46.740
Do you guys agree? I mean, I would definitely say so having not played this one with a zapper.

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:52.660
It's actually, I think maybe the first zapper game that I wasn't able to play with the actual hardware.

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:59.420
Um, but didn't we have other games in the past that, that played like this?

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:01.000
Yeah. I mean, maybe not.

00:08:01.480 --> 00:08:02.780
I don't know about both.

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:05.900
I thought it was that they involved the D pad.

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:08.420
It wasn't like you, you use the controller as well.

00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:14.180
I can't recall an example where you could choose to play entirely zapper or entirely controller.

00:08:14.520 --> 00:08:17.480
I gotcha. Um, but yeah, when I, but maybe that's true.

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:18.800
Maybe operation wolf was that.

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:20.420
Let me check. That's what I would have thought.

00:08:20.660 --> 00:08:22.600
But, um, who knows?

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:24.820
Cause I do throughout this game.

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:26.160
I did wonder the whole time.

00:08:26.200 --> 00:08:37.260
Like, I wonder what, what differences would be in my opinion, if I were able to play this with a zapper, because it was a little jarring to me to use the, uh, to use the D pad crosshair.

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:43.860
So I think with the, the, like the difference, I think there is some balance to it.

00:08:43.940 --> 00:08:48.500
I think that, yes, it is more, uh, intuitive to use the zapper.

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:56.720
Obviously you're just shooting at the screen, but the, the, that thing that I mentioned before, well, where it's all single shot with the zapper.

00:08:56.920 --> 00:09:08.420
I think that they tried to balance it a bit by giving you the ability to just sort of just lay waste with, I mean, it, it, that's also tempered by the fact that you have limited ammo though.

00:09:08.420 --> 00:09:10.040
You shouldn't really run out.

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:13.380
Um, but there's at least that consideration.

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:27.040
So operation wolf did let you use the controller.

00:09:27.280 --> 00:09:35.360
However, looking at it a little easier to control than the, and maybe I'm explaining this wrong, but you guys know what I mean?

00:09:35.360 --> 00:09:43.420
Like when you're playing it, it snaps so fast in the directions when you're playing with the NES controller on, on mechanized.

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:44.680
Yeah. You kind of need that.

00:09:44.720 --> 00:09:49.740
But then at the same time, it makes it really hard to like, the enemies are moving, you know?

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:51.160
So yeah, it makes it hard to stop.

00:09:51.300 --> 00:10:01.660
And therefore like a lot of times I, and you know, you have an Uzi, so whatever, like you're, you can rapid fire, you know, the ammo is technically limited, but there's a lot of it.

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:06.220
But I did find that my aim just wasn't great with a controller here.

00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:09.780
I think I improved as I went along.

00:10:10.120 --> 00:10:19.900
Um, I was getting a bit more twitchy with the thumb and finding the right line, um, to, to sort of do like a sweep.

00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:26.760
Um, and it's also, it also doesn't help that a lot of these enemies do require multiple shots to go down.

00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:32.500
Um, but it's, so yeah, it was hard, but I, it's not unplayable with a controller.

00:10:33.540 --> 00:10:41.200
Yeah. Uh, I also noticed that it could be somewhat forgiving as far as like, you don't have to be dead on.

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:50.000
I think that like part of the, the square of the crosshair has to be making contact with the hitbox, but like, you know, they don't have to be in your sights, I guess.

00:10:50.360 --> 00:10:52.340
If that doesn't have to be dead on, you're right.

00:10:52.340 --> 00:10:53.700
Yeah. It doesn't have to be dead on.

00:10:53.820 --> 00:11:02.240
